  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"1.0.0rc1\"\n\npackage:\n  name: pollen-bmi088-imu-library\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/p/pollen-BMI088-imu-library/pollen_bmi088_imu_library-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 6a82eafa448807a87c7a9e1ed8ef395b0ce5f2f57fa536b5b3a3f428e72d8fcf\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  # depends on smbus3 (unix-only I2C via /dev/i2c-*); unusable on Windows.\n  # Not noarch because conda-forge's linter forbids skips on noarch packages\n  # in staged-recipes; once this lives in its own feedstock it can become\n  # noarch: python with a `__unix` run dependency instead.\n  # python floor: ahrs needs >=3.10.\n  skip: win or match(python, \"<3.10\")\n  script: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python\n    - setuptools\n    - pip\n    # not used at build time, but forces rattler-build to build all python\n    # variants of smbus3 first; its deferred-test tracker matches by name only.\n    # Only needed while both recipes are staged together — remove once this\n    # recipe lives in its own feedstock.\n    - smbus3\n  run:\n    - python\n    - smbus3 ==0.5.5\n    - numpy >=2.2.5,<2.3.0\n    - ahrs\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - bmi088\n      pip_check: true\n\nabout:\n  # Upstream declares no license anywhere (neither the PyPI metadata nor the\n  # GitHub repository); assumed Apache-2.0 to match the rest of the Reachy\n  # stack. The sdist ships no license file either, so the recipe bundles the\n  # Apache-2.0 text (rattler-build falls back to the recipe directory for\n  # license_file).\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: BMI088 IMU library for Pollen Robotics hardware\n  description: |\n    Python library from Pollen Robotics for reading the Bosch BMI088\n    six-axis inertial measurement unit (accelerometer and gyroscope) over\n    I2C using smbus3, with sensor fusion for orientation estimation built\n    on the ahrs library. It is used for the IMU in the Reachy Mini robot.\n  homepage: https://pypi.org/project/pollen-bmi088-imu-library/\n  repository: https://github.com/pollen-robotics/pollen_BMI088_imu_library\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - ruben-arts\n",
